<exercisegroup cols="3" xml:id="exercisegroup-vector-geom-guess-orthog">
<title>Zero dot product</title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case,
	a vector <m> \uvec{u} </m> is provided.
	Use the guess-and-check method to determine a <em>nonzero</em> vector <m> \uvec{v} </m> so that <m> \udotprod{u}{v} = 0 </m>.
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (2,1) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> One possible answer is <m> \uvec{v} = (-1,2) </m>. </p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (3,-5) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> One possible answer is <m> \uvec{v} = (5,3) </m>. </p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (-2,-3,1) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> One possible answer is <m> \uvec{v} = (-1,1,1) </m>. </p></answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
